+# H-Angular-Momentum-In-The-Clicks-1 (ac1): the angular momentum read in the clicks alone (2026-10-26, 02:46 to 03:0x UTC; worktree at 910648f74, the records of 2ab32b518)
+
+Verdict line: **A FINDING.** The clicks conserve no angular momentum of their own and the law names none; what the clicks hold exactly is the identity with the board: the moment of the takes booked on the credit and birth lines, summed over a close, equals the board's change of the moment of the lattice momentum density across that close, to the integer and about any centre (the hole 60: 60 of 60 closes; the bodies 300: 300 of 300; the chiral 60: 56 of 60, the four misses the births whose children landed on standing light, where the record's one dP_lay cannot place a two-Node lay). The clicks' J and the board's L do not sum to a constant: between the closes the board's L walks by Rule3's torque and the swap (AM-S1's terms); the senses summed over a birth's children are 0 and are the charge, a scalar under the 48, not J's spin part.
+
+## 1. The algebra (from the law's letter)
+
+The reading. For every credit line J_credit(c) = (r - c) x dP_take, r the credited Node, dP_take the take's three integers (take.momentum_of: 2 num [d_now Gb_a + d_before Gn_a] per axis at one Node); for every birth line J_birth(c) = (r - c) x dP_take at the take's Node plus (r - c) x dP_lay for the children's lay (dP_lay the one vector the line carries, child_laid's sum over the two ends); the spin part the senses: the credit's `sense` and the two children's `senses`. Summed over a record it is what an observer reads at the detectors. In doubled coordinates about the board's centre, R = 2 r - (cube - 1), every arm is an integer and the reading is am2's L2 convention.
+
+The identity (derivable, no word needed). MV-S1's density p_a(i) lives on the Link i -> i + a and points along its axis a. A take at one Node z moves one line's level now by d levels and changes the currents of the two Links of each axis at z, (z - a, z) and (z, z + a), both along e_a; the moment of a current along e_a about any centre is the same from either end of its Link, (r_z - e_a - c) x e_a q = (r_z - c) x e_a q, and the same across the torus's seam, where the far end differs by (cube - 1) e_a. So the board's L changes across a one-Node take by exactly (r_z - c) x dP_take: the one-Node kick's moment is the moment of the board's momentum change, to the integer, the summation by parts needing no bulk (test_one_link_one_moment). The children's lay onto nothing carries one integer along its Link's axis (mk2's Theorem A) and the children's own form carries 0, so dP_lay = 0 and the lay's moment is 0 at every birth onto nothing (hole 16 of 16, ga2 64 of 64); where a child lands on standing light the lay moves the standing gradients' currents at two Nodes one Link apart and its moment needs the lay's momentum per end, which the birth line does not carry (the chiral: 9 of 17 births with dP_lay not 0, 4 with a child on standing light).
+
+What the law conserves of it. Across one close: the board's L(after the close) - L(before) = SUM over the close's clicks of (r - c) x (dP_take + dP_lay), exact, the remainder 0 (the identity above; MK-S2's along-axis remainder is not on the head, the recoil lay not entered; under it the along-axis part of r x (dP_take + dP_lay) would be cut to the remainder's moment and the transverse parts would stand). Across a birth: the two children's senses are -1 and +1, their sum 0 (W_children opposite), and their dP_lay sums to 0 onto nothing. Across a record: L_board(end) - L_board(start) = J_clicks(summed) + SUM over the intervals of the torque of Rule3's step and the swap (am2's dL2_step and dL2_swap; the writes 0); on the hole 60 the clicks' part is [-979035335222368732952, -851424732737678867128, 851424732737678867128] and the interval's acts' part [549511444423944906536, 875240056689162175248, -875240056689162175248], their sum the board's L2 at the end [-429523890798423826416, 23815323951483308120, -23815323951483308120] (am2's number reproduced on the head). Nothing in the clicks balances the clicks' J: it is the board's recoil read at the detectors, not a conserved quantity, exactly as nature's detectors read the recoil a target takes.
+
+The senses and J's spin part. The sense is the sign of the plane's Wronskian re_now im_before - im_now re_before at one Node, built from the plane's two internal lines; the 48 moves Nodes and Ports and leaves the four levels at a Node as they are, so the sense is a true scalar under the 48 (even under every reflection), odd under the plane's conjugation and under the exchange of now and before: a charge (gate 17 reads it so), one integer. J's spin part is a pseudovector, three integers, even under parity. So the senses' sum at births is the charge's conservation and not J's spin part; nature's unit of J in the clicks has no row on the head (no spinor-row world births; the light lay carries no sense), the shape-8 row's axial part unread by name.
+
+## 2. The measure (moment_of_clicks.py over the record's log, integers only; board_across_close.py the board's L2 before and after every close on the head's interval; compare_board.py the two against each other; out/)
